Package: qrme
Title: Quantile Regression with Measurement Error
Version: 1.0.1
Authors@R: c(person("Callaway", "Brantly", email = "brantly.callaway@uga.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")), person("Li", "Tong", email="tong.li@vanderbilt.edu", role="aut"), person("Murtazashvili", "Irina", email="im99@drexel.edu", role="aut"), person("Tsyawo", "Emmanuel S.", email="estsyawo@gmail.com", role="aut"))
Description: Code for estimating quantile regressions with measurement error.  The first main set of functions estimates quantile regression with measurement error in the dependent variable using an EM-type-algorithm.  The second set of functions estimates quantile regressions with measurement error in the outcome and in a continuous "treatment" variable.  All functions allow for an arbitrary number of other covariates that are assumed not to be measured with error.
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://bcallaway11.github.io/qrme, https://github.com/bcallaway11/qrme
BugReports: https://github.com/bcallaway11/qrme/issues
Imports: BMisc, copula, ggplot2, mixtools, pbapply, quantreg, tidyr, gumbel, Rcpp
LinkingTo: Rcpp, RcppArmadillo
Suggests: quarto, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
